This reference includes qyl, vendor, upstream OpenTelemetry core and GenAI definitions at every resolved stability,
including development, experimental producer paths and explicitly deprecated definitions. Each group identifies
its source and schema. Upstream ownership is preserved; inclusion does not make upstream definitions qyl-owned.
Registry schema URLs identify these definitions; they do not assert that native producers advertise those URLs in OTLP.

Native vendor definitions describe the producer's actual keys, units and routing. qyl's agent-observability
definitions specify the development contract for cross-producer adapters. A registry declaration does not
establish that an adapter is deployed or that a particular record reached a collector. Native exceptions to
recommended OTel naming or units are documented rather than hidden by changing the wire contract.

Entity identity is separate from descriptive attributes. Identifying fields have no requirement level in
Weaver 0.28.0's materialized entity model. Signal attributes retain their own requirement levels.

